# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# A merge whose model reads a free name, held and called. add reads other,
# a field of the unit, 9. w holds merge(y: 5; add) and u merge(y: 100; add):
# the node a merge builds has its own contract, the formal the merge leaves
# unbound and then the model's free name, and its body reads each at its
# place there. From the root: 5 + 1 + 9, and 100 + 1 + 9. under has other
# 20: the caller's value reaches the node, 26. Entry 7.
int: other 9

fn: add (int: y; int: x) int
    return: y + x + other

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    return: merge(y: k; add)

@: w wrap(5)
@: u wrap(100)

fn: under () int
    int: other 20
    return: (w: 1)
end: under

int: a (w: 1)
int: b (u: 1)
int: c under()
int: ok 7
if: a != 15 || b != 110 || c != 26
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
